 ### Question
 
 How does the operator inspect and control raw-AV discard, summaries, hashes, clips and any permitted subsequent export?
 
 ### Current direction
 
-Delta §17.9. Controls must show capture state, destination and retention effects, obey hard Compartment denials and preserve minimized correction/deletion metadata. Hashes and summaries can still expose sensitive context; no blanket permission to export them follows from deleting raw media.
+Delta §17.9. `UBU-D0328` specifies policy-filtered capture/artifact inspection and independent discard, summary, optional hash, clip and export controls in DESIGN.md §12.2. Derivative retention needs its own explicit purpose/destination/retention approval; permitted exports require final content/metadata review, operation-bound approval and current authority/policy checks. Hard denials and minimized append-only correction/deletion metadata remain binding.
 
 ### Resolution
 
-Open.
+Resolved by `UBU-D0328`: DESIGN.md §12.2 defines inspection, independent artifact actions, separately approved derivative retention and export, version-bound review, cancellation/restart, policy-safe audit and truthful cleanup/delivery status. Summaries and hashes inherit source restrictions; raw deletion never grants export or edits admitted claims. Revision-pinned denial, stale-approval, lifecycle and egress fixtures are required before enablement. This resolves the operator-control contract, not implementation or physical erasure; `UBU-Q0168`, `UBU-Q0177` and `UBU-Q0162` retain measured-performance, hardware and Log-enforcement scope.
 
